The user’s explicit constraints were to avoid destructive changes, avoid replacing or deleting existing major assets prematurely, keep the dedicated TCP server separate from Unity Services/Relay/Netcode, and stop before gameplay/question loops or result logic. The work therefore emphasized compile-valid server code, data-model safety, and UI scaffolding rather than runtime gameplay features.
